# Import / publish / merge system rules (КРУГИ)

Standing gates from the Jul 2026 backlog — do not re-introduce one-off workarounds.

## Merge (R01)
- Fill-empty / union only; never overwrite non-empty keep fields (including `image_url`).
- Catalog donor is **destroyed** after merge (hard delete); archive only if FK blocks delete.
- Merge never auto-publishes — archived → `pending` at most; Approve is separate.
- Queue twins stay `status=duplicate`.
- Shared phone / ad-account cluster (Оксана / Katia / Viktor on one number): **one keeper**, donors only fill-empty contacts/copy/media — do not mint parallel profiles.

## Catalog target pick (R15) — merge-all
- Source of truth: `pickBestCatalogMergeTarget` in `lib/import-review/merge-contract.ts`.
- Score: approved(+phone) ≫ approved ≫ pending ≫ archived across **both** businesses and professionals.
- Never prefer archived business over approved professional (same phone) — that caused public `/business/…` 404 while live specialist existed.
- Same score → prefer `professional`.
- Duplicate list order uses `duplicateMatchListRank` (approved first, archived last).

## Public href after merge (R16)
- `liveEntityHref` returns `/business|/professional` **only** when `status=approved`.
- Pending/archived → `null` (no redirect into public 404).
- Source: `isPubliclyListedStatus` + `lib/import-review/live-entity-href.ts`.

## Enrich SaaS (R02 / R08)
- `PLATFORM_SAAS_HOSTS` / `isPlatformSaasHost`: dikidi, glossgenius, fresha, vagaro, booksy, calendly, …
- SaaS URL → `booking_url` only; never card `website` / platform phone / `@dikidi.` email / platform IG.
- Keep TS (`lib/import-review/platform-saas-hosts.ts`) and Python (`scripts/business-enrich/platform_saas_hosts.py`) in sync.

## Street + geo (R03 / R04)
- No street → not `businesses` (specialist or skip). Enforce on approve **and** autopublish.
- Never default `city` / service_area to `"Orange County"`.

## Recommendations (R05)
- Third-party reco without self-offer → attach/suspect only; do not create new approved entity.

## Events (R06 / R07)
- `purge_past_events(10, 30)` in `run_scheduled_maintenance`.
- Multi-date posts: split to N events or block approve until structured.

## Categories (R09 / R10)
- Ban publish with `pro_other` / missing professional category.
- `celebrations` / `party_planning` → business|specialist by street, never affiche `events` table.
- `category=events` → affiche only with date signal.

## Content (R12 / R13)
- Approve runs `redactContactsFromPublicText` on description.
- News / office-move → updates via `isNewsUpdateTitle`, never services.

## Hard publish firewall (R17)
- Source: `lib/import-review/publish-firewall.ts` (`assertPublishAllowed`).
- **Additive only** — existing enrich/merge/approve paths stay; firewall only blocks bad publishes.
- Runs on Approve (and must stay on autopublish). LLM may suggest; firewall decides.
- Money transfer / lechu / goods / jobs — cannot publish into wrong section (router high-confidence mismatch → block + rewrite hint).
- Strong hiring / CDL ads → `jobs`, not specialist/business.
- No street / **HTML-CMS garbage street** (`isGarbageStreetLine`) → not `businesses`.
- Specialist: ban `pro_other` / empty category; repair text cannot sit in `legal`.
- Biz→pro category remap: `lib/import-review/category-slug-map.ts` (does not delete categories).
- Shared-phone ad clusters → one keeper (see R01/R15), donors fill-empty only.
- Catalog backfill (additive, separate from queue Enrich): `scripts/business-enrich/run_catalog_backfill_enrich.py` wraps existing published enrich scripts; does not change `run_pre_publish_enrich.py`.

